  fonts/ — Manrope and Young Serif, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1;
  see fonts/LICENSE.txt.

They are bundled here so the app presents the same interface. Every /api/...
request they make is answered by the Kotlin implementation in :core rather than
by the Node server they were written against. Endpoints this build does not
implement answer in the UI's own "feature is off" shape, so no screen is left
in an error state.

THEY ARE NOT A VERBATIM COPY, and have not been since 0.1.x. This build removes
what a phone cannot serve (labels, Qobuz and TIDAL accounts, the wall display,
waveforms), adds what only it has (playlists you make yourself, the artists
wall, the Network pane, grouped Pitchfork, the dial), and keeps a few rules
Rouen does not (it never polls, the Home draws are the same all day). So a newer
Rouen is a THREE-WAY MERGE, not a copy:

  UPSTREAM BASE: meltface-80/Rouen affea8c (v1.8.84, 2026-10-07)

  base   = git show a1daa61:public/<file>        (in a Rouen clone)
  ours   = this directory
  theirs = the newer Rouen public/<file>
  git merge-file -p --diff3 ours base theirs

Then update the commit above. The bases before it were Rouen a1daa61
(v1.8.77) and MusicD-Remote 40f02f1 (v1.7.70), and sharecard.js separately
bdc1a0c (v1.7.89). HQPlayer control (Rouen v1.8.74–v1.8.78) is left out of
this build, page and server both.

  icons/rouen-tile.png — the Rouen tile the share card draws in its corner,
  from Rouen's icons/ unchanged.

dial.html and dial.js are this app's own, a page version of the dial.
